WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.835
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:06.105 --> 00:08.265
Have you never felt anything for me?

3
00:08.345 --> 00:09.465
You're my client.

4
00:09.545 --> 00:11.705
Then when you kissed me and slept with me,

5
00:11.785 --> 00:13.425
was all of it just for work?

6
00:13.505 --> 00:16.065
Rakkhun is hurting because of you right now.

7
00:16.145 --> 00:17.705
Rakkhun loves you.

8
00:19.825 --> 00:21.225
Vann!

9
00:22.145 --> 00:23.505
I want to be your boyfriend.

10
00:23.585 --> 00:25.865
Rakkhun, will you be my boyfriend?

11
00:26.465 --> 00:28.025
You're going to sing here?

12
00:28.105 --> 00:30.265
I'm offering myself to test things out first.

13
00:30.345 --> 00:32.544
If we end up in the same band,

14
00:32.625 --> 00:35.225
we'll know whether our voices work well together.

15
00:35.305 --> 00:36.025
Okay?

16
01:08.105 --> 01:12.625
I’ve been looking at you for so long

17
01:12.705 --> 01:15.305
I don't dare to look

18
01:16.265 --> 01:18.745
I always have to avoid your eyes

19
01:18.825 --> 01:22.865
I’m afraid that one day

20
01:22.945 --> 01:26.585
If you find out

21
01:26.665 --> 01:31.265
The truth I’ve been hiding away

22
01:31.865 --> 01:37.225
The secret I’ve hidden I’ve never told anyone

23
01:37.305 --> 01:42.265
I don't think I can hold it back anymore

24
01:43.785 --> 01:49.265
The closer I am to you, The more I want to reveal my heart

25
01:49.345 --> 01:54.225
When we make eye contact My heart shakes even more

26
01:54.305 --> 02:00.185
It’s just too hard To keep this love hidden away

27
02:00.265 --> 02:05.865
And the secret inside your heart Does it include me at all?

28
02:05.945 --> 02:12.785
Please tell me what’s in your heart Let me know

29
02:17.425 --> 02:18.465
See?

30
02:19.065 --> 02:21.425
See how well we sing together?

31
02:22.025 --> 02:23.825
Please audition for our band.

32
02:28.825 --> 02:31.825
What do you say? Can you do it for me?

33
02:32.545 --> 02:35.585
Phatee, you're the first person I've ever begged like this.

34
02:39.905 --> 02:41.105
Phatee!

35
02:42.945 --> 02:44.585
Phatee!

36
02:44.665 --> 02:46.425
Phatee!

37
02:54.905 --> 02:56.145
Phatee!

38
02:57.985 --> 02:59.705
Phatee!

39
03:05.025 --> 03:06.025
Damn.

40
03:06.105 --> 03:09.145
I thought you were fucking dead. I've been calling you forever.

41
03:09.745 --> 03:10.945
What do you want?

42
03:11.025 --> 03:14.105
Linda sent me to get you. Looks like there's a job.

43
03:15.545 --> 03:16.465
I'll be there.

44
03:17.385 --> 03:18.705
Okay.

45
03:39.825 --> 03:40.985
It was just a dream.

46
03:42.465 --> 03:44.945
Why did it feel so damn good?

47
04:52.945 --> 04:55.265
PJ, add the keyboard sync this time.

48
04:55.345 --> 04:56.345
I'll handle it.

49
04:56.905 --> 04:58.025
I'll add the bass.

50
04:58.105 --> 04:59.025
Got it.

51
04:59.705 --> 05:01.065
Let's rehearse one more time.

52
05:01.145 --> 05:02.345
Come on, Saw.

53
05:07.585 --> 05:09.305
That's enough for today.

54
05:11.345 --> 05:12.465
Kao.

55
05:12.545 --> 05:14.985
We booked the rehearsal room until this evening.

56
05:15.065 --> 05:16.385
Check the system first.

57
05:16.985 --> 05:19.185
I canceled your rehearsal room myself.

58
05:22.145 --> 05:23.865
What do you mean?

59
05:23.945 --> 05:26.345
Someone needs the rehearsal room more.

60
05:28.025 --> 05:29.745
They're a new group of trainees

61
05:29.825 --> 05:31.985
scheduled to debut next week.

62
05:32.065 --> 05:34.025
So I had to let them use the rehearsal room first.

63
05:34.905 --> 05:36.065
You guys can head over there.

64
05:40.745 --> 05:41.665
Kao.

65
05:41.745 --> 05:43.945
We've been waiting to debut for ages too.

66
05:45.225 --> 05:46.585
I already told you.

67
05:46.665 --> 05:49.745
If you still can't find a main vocalist with a distinctive voice,

68
05:49.825 --> 05:52.465
I don't see why you should debut.

69
05:52.545 --> 05:54.385
There's no selling point.

70
05:55.185 --> 05:57.185
You guys can leave now. Go.

71
06:00.865 --> 06:03.465
Wait until they're gone, then you can start rehearsing.

72
06:21.665 --> 06:22.945
Fuck!

73
06:25.625 --> 06:27.025
Don't take it out on me.

74
06:27.105 --> 06:28.305
I think

75
06:28.985 --> 06:30.585
if this keeps up,

76
06:30.665 --> 06:32.225
we won't just lose rehearsal time.

77
06:33.025 --> 06:35.585
They might even stop us from using the rehearsal room altogether.

78
06:37.305 --> 06:38.305
Exactly.

79
06:39.665 --> 06:42.265
What about that great guy you said you want in the band?

80
06:42.345 --> 06:45.745
What did he say? If he doesn't join, we'll have to change the plan.

81
06:46.385 --> 06:47.385
No.

82
06:48.345 --> 06:49.705
Trust me.

83
06:50.265 --> 06:53.945
This time, he'll definitely say yes.

84
07:03.265 --> 07:05.625
Linda, I think I found the client.

85
07:06.505 --> 07:08.385
The client's name is Cherry, right?

86
07:08.465 --> 07:10.105
No, her name is Lilly.

87
07:10.185 --> 07:11.745
Take good care of her.

88
07:11.825 --> 07:12.825
And smile.

89
07:12.905 --> 07:13.985
Okay.

90
07:24.745 --> 07:27.345
I'm Phatee from The Crow Club.

91
07:29.985 --> 07:31.745
You're Lilly, our client, right?

92
07:31.825 --> 07:32.745
Oh.

93
07:32.825 --> 07:35.425
Yes, but I'm not your client.

94
07:35.505 --> 07:38.185
I'm just the middleman who contacted The Crow Club.

95
07:38.265 --> 07:39.505
The one who hired you

96
07:40.185 --> 07:41.105
is that guy.

97
07:41.985 --> 07:42.865
You.

98
07:45.745 --> 07:46.825
Uh…

99
07:48.145 --> 07:50.785
Now that you've met, I'll get going.

100
07:57.705 --> 07:58.705
Hey.

101
07:59.545 --> 08:00.545
Hey, wait.

102
08:01.105 --> 08:03.465
Hey, I already paid Linda.

103
08:03.545 --> 08:04.785
Hey.

104
08:04.865 --> 08:06.425
I'll have Linda refund you.

105
08:07.025 --> 08:08.665
Today's job is simple.

106
08:09.265 --> 08:10.745
I won't ask you to do anything else.

107
08:12.185 --> 08:15.225
But if you want to do something else,

108
08:15.305 --> 08:16.465
I wouldn't mind.

109
08:19.585 --> 08:21.105
Hey, I'm kidding.

110
08:22.145 --> 08:22.985
How about this?

111
08:23.705 --> 08:26.305
If you take the job and go shopping with me today,

112
08:26.825 --> 08:28.065
I promise

113
08:28.145 --> 08:30.865
I won't bother you about the audition again.

114
08:31.545 --> 08:34.105
Whatever you decide, it's up to you.

115
08:36.784 --> 08:37.784
Are you in?

116
08:43.825 --> 08:45.465
What kind of music do you usually listen to?

117
08:46.225 --> 08:47.585
I listen to anything.

118
08:47.665 --> 08:51.065
Rock. Pop rock. Indie rock.

119
08:51.145 --> 08:53.185
What do you mean, anything? That's all rock.

120
08:54.145 --> 08:56.385
So, do you have a favorite band?

121
08:58.545 --> 08:59.985
Hey.

122
09:00.065 --> 09:01.345
You can answer me.

123
09:01.425 --> 09:03.065
Even if you lie, I won't know.

124
09:03.905 --> 09:05.705
I have to make some conversation.

125
09:06.385 --> 09:07.985
Otherwise it'll get awkward.

126
09:12.345 --> 09:13.345
"Pause."

127
09:15.105 --> 09:15.985
Hey.

128
09:16.065 --> 09:17.745
You've got good taste.

129
09:17.825 --> 09:18.985
What's your favorite song?

130
09:24.505 --> 09:25.505
"Secret."

131
09:35.825 --> 09:36.865
Let's check out this store.

132
09:41.825 --> 09:43.065
Is this necklace pretty?

133
09:43.145 --> 09:44.145
It is.

134
09:47.345 --> 09:48.825
That store has nice clothes too.

135
09:48.905 --> 09:49.985
Let's go look.

136
09:51.705 --> 09:53.505
What's your dream?

137
09:53.585 --> 09:55.945
Where do you want to go, or what do you want to do?

138
09:56.665 --> 09:59.225
Let's make it simple. What do you like doing?

139
10:01.145 --> 10:02.145
Nothing.

140
10:02.825 --> 10:05.385
If it's what I like doing most, I guess playing guitar.

141
10:08.785 --> 10:10.905
Hey. Come here.

142
10:15.025 --> 10:16.625
I think

143
10:18.025 --> 10:20.625
this shirt would look good on you.

144
10:23.385 --> 10:24.985
Try it on for me.

145
10:26.025 --> 10:27.025
Please?

146
10:27.625 --> 10:29.145
Come on, try it on.

147
10:29.225 --> 10:30.225
I'll help.

148
10:30.745 --> 10:32.305
I'll do it myself.

149
10:47.665 --> 10:49.505
Come on. Hurry up.

150
11:05.145 --> 11:07.745
Don't you ever think about taking music seriously?

151
11:08.785 --> 11:10.145
You don't have to convince me.

152
11:11.305 --> 11:12.825
Even if you try all day, you won't succeed.

153
11:20.945 --> 11:22.105
Huh.

154
11:31.305 --> 11:33.545
Hey. Hold this shirt up for me.

155
11:34.545 --> 11:35.505
Come on.

156
11:39.545 --> 11:40.745
I'll take this one.

157
11:41.905 --> 11:42.945
I'm really good at this.

158
11:44.305 --> 11:46.385
You can wear this denim shirt.

159
11:46.465 --> 11:47.745
You'll look cool.

160
11:48.625 --> 11:49.705
Cool like me.

161
11:51.985 --> 11:52.985
Let's go.

162
11:58.185 --> 11:59.745
Where are you going?

163
12:01.545 --> 12:02.745
That sounds so damn good.

164
12:04.865 --> 12:05.865
Come here.

165
12:07.225 --> 12:08.265
Follow me.

166
12:17.305 --> 12:18.545
What are you doing?

167
12:18.625 --> 12:19.905
Hey.

168
12:19.985 --> 12:21.065
Come on.

169
12:22.665 --> 12:26.585
The time I hired you for today isn't up yet, right?

170
12:27.145 --> 12:28.705
Consider this part of the job.

171
12:32.145 --> 12:33.065
Uh…

172
12:33.145 --> 12:34.105
Excuse me.

173
12:34.185 --> 12:36.225
-Can I borrow your guitar? -Sure.

174
12:38.985 --> 12:39.985
Thanks.

175
12:42.185 --> 12:43.985
Here. Take it.

176
12:45.625 --> 12:47.745
Play whichever song you like best.

177
12:47.825 --> 12:48.865
I'll follow your lead.

178
12:51.465 --> 12:52.665
Here, take it.

179
13:02.065 --> 13:02.905
Like this.

180
13:08.985 --> 13:09.985
Come on.

181
13:12.385 --> 13:13.505
Hey.

182
13:16.705 --> 13:18.305
If you don't know where to look,

183
13:19.705 --> 13:20.985
look at me.

184
13:33.425 --> 13:34.825
-Hey. -Yeah?

185
13:35.665 --> 13:37.585
Can you play the backing track for me?

186
13:37.665 --> 13:38.665
Sure.

187
13:56.185 --> 14:00.265
I’ve been looking at you for so long

188
14:00.345 --> 14:06.585
I don't dare to look I always have to avoid your eyes

189
14:06.665 --> 14:10.905
I’m afraid that one day

190
14:10.985 --> 14:14.385
If you find out

191
14:14.465 --> 14:18.505
the truth I’ve been hiding away

192
14:19.585 --> 14:25.025
The secret I’ve hidden I’ve never told anyone

193
14:25.105 --> 14:28.825
I don't think I can hold it back anymore

194
14:29.785 --> 14:35.025
The closer I am to you The more I want to reveal my heart

195
14:35.105 --> 14:40.305
When we make eye contact My heart shakes even more

196
14:40.385 --> 14:45.865
It’s just too hard To keep this love hidden away

197
14:45.945 --> 14:51.625
And the secret inside your heart, Does it include me at all?

198
14:51.705 --> 14:54.385
Please tell me

199
14:54.465 --> 14:59.545
What’s in your heart, let me know

200
15:08.065 --> 15:12.225
I take your words

201
15:12.305 --> 15:14.545
And overthink them

202
15:15.745 --> 15:18.545
Secretly imagining things All by myself like this

203
15:18.625 --> 15:23.025
Because you… You are just so incredibly good

204
15:23.105 --> 15:26.265
How much longer

205
15:26.345 --> 15:31.625
Do I have to keep The words "I love you" inside?

206
15:31.705 --> 15:37.025
The secret I’ve hidden I’ve never told anyone

207
15:37.105 --> 15:41.625
I don't think I can hold it back anymore

208
15:41.705 --> 15:47.025
The closer I am to you The more I want to reveal my heart

209
15:47.105 --> 15:52.025
When we make eye contact My heart shakes even more

210
15:52.105 --> 15:57.905
It’s just too hard To keep this love hidden away

211
15:57.985 --> 16:03.625
And the secret inside your heart Does it include me at all?

212
16:03.705 --> 16:06.345
Please tell me

213
16:06.425 --> 16:11.825
What’s in your heart, let me know

214
16:40.105 --> 16:41.505
See? You can do it.

215
17:04.464 --> 17:06.745
Why are you sitting at the bar today, Mr. Writer?

216
17:06.825 --> 17:08.464
Don't act like we're close.

217
17:08.545 --> 17:10.224
You wouldn't take the job when I asked you to be my boyfriend.

218
17:11.585 --> 17:13.105
You're awful.

219
17:13.944 --> 17:15.745
When someone hits on you, you reject him.

220
17:17.305 --> 17:19.385
Then when the guy pursuing you tries to leave,

221
17:19.464 --> 17:21.345
you casually pull him back in.

222
17:22.585 --> 17:23.505
That's not very nice.

223
17:27.184 --> 17:30.785
But it's just like the protagonist in my novel.

224
17:31.825 --> 17:34.665
I like that kind of push-and-pull.

225
17:37.585 --> 17:40.585
I just wanted to know why you're sitting at the bar today.

226
17:42.025 --> 17:44.145
I just wanted a change of perspective.

227
17:44.985 --> 17:46.425
Maybe I'll get an idea

228
17:47.305 --> 17:48.785
of what the male lead in the novel

229
17:48.865 --> 17:50.105
would do

230
17:50.625 --> 17:52.425
if the other person disappeared.

231
17:55.585 --> 17:57.705
Does it have to follow the formula that closely?

232
18:02.545 --> 18:03.545
Today,

233
18:04.425 --> 18:07.545
there aren't many customers because Phatee isn't singing.

234
18:08.905 --> 18:10.025
So I'm free.

235
18:12.265 --> 18:13.185
Actually,

236
18:13.905 --> 18:18.905
I'm wondering if I should give up and find a new male lead.

237
18:24.225 --> 18:25.225
So?

238
18:25.945 --> 18:27.145
Did you find one?

239
18:28.265 --> 18:30.865
But I might have to switch from sweet romance

240
18:30.945 --> 18:32.185
to another genre.

241
18:33.025 --> 18:34.545
Like

242
18:35.305 --> 18:36.585
something

243
18:37.185 --> 18:38.705
with a warning.

244
18:38.785 --> 18:40.545
NSFW or something.

245
18:53.985 --> 18:55.545
Someone once told me

246
18:55.625 --> 18:57.825
if I can't write the story I want right now,

247
18:57.905 --> 18:59.425
I should write something else in the meantime.

248
19:02.345 --> 19:03.625
Adult fiction

249
19:04.825 --> 19:05.825
isn't so bad.

250
19:08.265 --> 19:09.345
What kind

251
19:10.345 --> 19:11.345
of adult fiction?

252
19:12.065 --> 19:13.145
Murder?

253
19:14.985 --> 19:16.145
Probably not.

254
19:18.665 --> 19:20.425
Want to have some fun with adult fiction?

255
19:23.425 --> 19:24.905
I'm not hiring you for this.

256
19:25.985 --> 19:27.225
I'm just asking if you're interested.

257
20:12.505 --> 20:13.505
So?

258
20:14.305 --> 20:15.785
Interesting enough?

259
20:26.665 --> 20:28.785
Well, fortune teller? Your client asked.

260
20:28.865 --> 20:30.665
So, is Vann secretly seeing someone else?

261
20:32.785 --> 20:34.305
He doesn't have someone else, right?

262
20:34.385 --> 20:35.945
I'm sure he doesn't.

263
20:36.505 --> 20:39.945
But he's so handsome. Someone might approach him.

264
20:40.025 --> 20:42.265
I've already gone through three decks.

265
20:43.505 --> 20:44.745
Hey, listen to me.

266
20:44.825 --> 20:50.105
Vann doesn't have the time or the means to find someone else.

267
20:51.065 --> 20:52.065
I believe you.

268
20:53.105 --> 20:54.545
I just want to be sure.

269
20:56.705 --> 20:58.025
Want to do a fourth deck, fortune teller?

270
20:58.105 --> 21:00.985
We've gone through them all.

271
21:08.145 --> 21:10.625
Mimi, what's wrong? You look so sad.

272
21:11.385 --> 21:12.825
-Nay. -What?

273
21:12.905 --> 21:14.785
Stop reading cards for Vann and Rakkhun.

274
21:14.865 --> 21:16.465
Do a love reading for me instead.

275
21:18.705 --> 21:22.305
I'm hurt. Talay broke my heart.

276
21:23.625 --> 21:26.625
Talay doesn't even allow you to like him, Mimi.

277
21:26.705 --> 21:29.545
The first rule of The Crow Club:

278
21:29.625 --> 21:31.905
Anyone who works here can't like Talay.

279
21:35.345 --> 21:37.385
But Talay can like the writer? Is that it?

280
21:39.185 --> 21:41.465
Then should I just quit?

281
21:41.545 --> 21:43.785
Then I can hit on Talay without breaking the rules.

282
21:48.785 --> 21:50.105
-What? What's wrong? -Snap! Crack!

283
21:50.185 --> 21:51.585
Snap! Boom!

284
21:53.105 --> 21:54.705
Did you guys hear that strange sound?

285
21:54.785 --> 21:56.065
What sound?

286
21:58.025 --> 21:59.825
The sound of my heart.

287
21:59.905 --> 22:01.865
Talay broke it.

288
22:02.825 --> 22:03.905
If you weren't here,

289
22:04.585 --> 22:06.425
I'd be hurt and lonely all by myself.

290
22:06.505 --> 22:08.465
I'm lucky to have you hurting with me.

291
22:10.625 --> 22:13.545
But you know, right? Once Talay goes home,

292
22:14.305 --> 22:16.385
you'll have to watch the place alone all night.

293
22:16.465 --> 22:18.825
-What? How can Talay go home? -There.

294
22:19.665 --> 22:22.425
-Hey! -"Rule number one."

295
22:23.465 --> 22:24.745
Talay.

296
22:26.065 --> 22:27.665
Take my car.

297
22:27.745 --> 22:28.905
Are we going to your place?

298
22:29.745 --> 22:30.705
Who said you could?

299
22:30.785 --> 22:31.905
Don't get your hopes up.

300
22:33.345 --> 22:34.945
Why can't I go to your place?

301
22:35.505 --> 22:36.625
What are you hiding?

302
22:37.345 --> 22:38.905
I'm a romance novelist.

303
22:38.985 --> 22:41.785
I never let anyone come over except someone special to me.

304
22:41.865 --> 22:42.745
And I'll…

305
22:44.945 --> 22:46.105
probably never meet anyone.

306
22:48.425 --> 22:49.785
Hey!

307
22:49.865 --> 22:50.865
Talay.

308
22:53.105 --> 22:54.185
Where are you going?

309
22:54.265 --> 22:55.785
It's your shift today.

310
22:56.665 --> 22:58.465
Why can't I go?

311
22:58.545 --> 22:59.865
Well,

312
23:00.465 --> 23:03.025
who's going to supervise the delivery guys?

313
23:05.505 --> 23:06.905
You're afraid to see the delivery guy.

314
23:08.265 --> 23:10.105
Be brave, Tangmo.

315
23:10.185 --> 23:11.785
You're just seeing your ex.

316
23:14.065 --> 23:15.425
Want to put that in your novel?

317
23:16.265 --> 23:17.665
A guy who is in denial

318
23:17.745 --> 23:19.785
and keeps running into his ex,

319
23:19.865 --> 23:21.025
who he's still not over.

320
23:21.745 --> 23:22.785
What ex?

321
23:23.505 --> 23:24.905
Just a friend.

322
23:25.625 --> 23:26.505
No.

323
23:27.185 --> 23:28.865
He's just someone I used to know.

324
23:28.945 --> 23:30.265
That's all?

325
23:30.345 --> 23:31.425
Then you can stay for the delivery.

326
23:31.505 --> 23:33.145
Talay.

327
23:34.465 --> 23:38.265
Someone who won't admit how he feels needs to be taught a lesson sometimes.

328
23:39.465 --> 23:40.785
-I'm leaving. -Hey.

329
23:40.865 --> 23:42.145
Go ahead, Mr. Writer.

330
24:23.025 --> 24:24.305
That's all.

331
24:25.745 --> 24:27.345
You don't actually have to help me.

332
24:28.065 --> 24:28.905
I'll carry it myself.

333
24:28.985 --> 24:30.825
What? Who's helping you?

334
24:30.905 --> 24:32.425
I'm not helping.

335
24:32.505 --> 24:35.505
I'm just tired of waiting for you. You're too slow.

336
24:36.185 --> 24:37.985
You're so skinny and scrawny.

337
24:38.065 --> 24:40.905
It'll take you till your next life to finish carrying this stuff.

338
24:43.185 --> 24:46.385
So that's the only reason. You're not worried about me at all.

339
24:46.465 --> 24:49.265
Right. When you're done, bring me the bill.

340
24:49.345 --> 24:51.065
Then you can finally leave.

341
25:07.585 --> 25:08.745
What happened to your hand?

342
25:09.945 --> 25:11.385
Who did this to you? Tell me.

343
25:12.145 --> 25:13.385
No one did anything to me.

344
25:13.465 --> 25:16.785
I was just clumsy doing delivery work this morning.

345
25:31.185 --> 25:34.785
Stop taking delivery jobs, delivering and carrying stuff.

346
25:34.865 --> 25:36.705
Can you just focus on rehearsing with me?

347
25:37.465 --> 25:40.465
If you're going to compete, you can't treat your body like this.

348
25:40.545 --> 25:42.585
Why do you care about me?

349
25:44.985 --> 25:45.985
Yoyeh.

350
25:46.825 --> 25:50.025
You're the one who wants to win that fucking reality show.

351
25:50.785 --> 25:53.745
If you want to win, focus on one thing at a time.

352
25:56.985 --> 26:00.105
But I need money to survive until the competition, don't I?

353
26:01.585 --> 26:03.105
What if I give you that money?

354
26:04.705 --> 26:06.625
Will you focus on rehearsing with me?

355
26:09.025 --> 26:10.305
Give me your QR code.

356
26:13.905 --> 26:15.305
You ran away from home to live alone.

357
26:16.305 --> 26:17.585
Don't you need money too?

358
26:17.665 --> 26:19.625
Give me your QR code.

359
26:34.345 --> 26:36.625
I don't have money to throw around like when I lived with Dad.

360
26:37.185 --> 26:38.745
But it's not like I'm broke.

361
26:39.985 --> 26:41.945
You can have last month's salary.

362
26:42.545 --> 26:45.065
You still love splurging on people, just like when you were a kid.

363
26:45.905 --> 26:48.385
I'm not that little kid who followed you around anymore.

364
26:48.465 --> 26:50.705
I'm not splurging on you.

365
26:50.785 --> 26:53.545
Consider it payment for helping out at the shop.

366
26:53.625 --> 26:56.785
Talay is too busy to help me anyway.

367
26:58.505 --> 27:01.905
You haven't changed at all. You always do things without asking me.

368
27:01.985 --> 27:03.065
Are you insulting me?

369
27:03.145 --> 27:05.425
Then I take it back. Transfer the money back to me.

370
27:05.505 --> 27:06.585
No.

371
27:07.425 --> 27:08.825
Your offer is good.

372
27:09.425 --> 27:11.785
I'll help out at your shop instead.

373
27:11.865 --> 27:13.305
But I want to be paid daily.

374
27:26.865 --> 27:28.745
BALANCE: 3,259.50 BAHT

375
27:28.825 --> 27:30.105
Damn it.

376
27:30.185 --> 27:32.025
Shit, I've only got 3,000 baht left.

377
27:47.345 --> 27:48.865
You're back late.

378
27:48.945 --> 27:51.065
Linda said you'd finish work in the evening.

379
27:53.145 --> 27:54.785
You must've enjoyed being a paid companion.

380
27:55.625 --> 27:57.905
Want to take over Vann's jobs, then?

381
27:57.985 --> 27:59.145
No.

382
28:16.865 --> 28:18.345
What the hell is wrong with you?

383
28:18.425 --> 28:19.945
Standing there smiling to yourself.

384
28:20.025 --> 28:21.625
Did Garlah's ghost possess you?

385
28:23.625 --> 28:24.625
No.

386
28:26.305 --> 28:27.545
Something's weird about you.

387
28:27.625 --> 28:28.745
You're not acting normal.

388
28:30.225 --> 28:31.665
Fortune teller!

389
28:31.745 --> 28:33.385
Read his fortune.

390
28:33.465 --> 28:34.705
See who put a spell on him.

391
28:34.785 --> 28:36.185
Let's do it, Bro.

392
28:36.265 --> 28:38.265
Come here. Let's read your fortune.

393
28:39.465 --> 28:41.425
We'll know once I draw the cards.

394
28:49.705 --> 28:52.065
No one's put a spell on you.

395
28:52.145 --> 28:53.505
But lately,

396
28:54.105 --> 28:57.025
it looks like you'll encounter something that

397
28:57.105 --> 28:59.705
makes your heart flutter.

398
28:59.785 --> 29:01.425
His heart will flutter?

399
29:01.505 --> 29:02.905
Well?

400
29:03.465 --> 29:05.185
Anything you want to tell me?

401
29:05.745 --> 29:07.385
Maybe it'll cheer me up too.

402
29:09.825 --> 29:10.825
No.

403
29:12.665 --> 29:13.745
You sure?

404
29:14.345 --> 29:15.465
Yeah.

405
29:16.705 --> 29:18.385
If I ask you about love,

406
29:18.465 --> 29:19.705
could you even answer me?

407
29:19.785 --> 29:21.705
You brat. You're fine when you're quiet,

408
29:21.785 --> 29:23.265
but when you talk, you always pick a fight.

409
29:23.345 --> 29:25.265
Why did you decide to take the job?

410
29:25.865 --> 29:27.225
Because you like him, right?

411
29:30.545 --> 29:34.505
If you don't want to see your ex, you shouldn't have taken the job.

412
29:35.185 --> 29:37.705
Who the fuck started saying he's my ex?

413
29:37.785 --> 29:38.705
Linda and Mimi.

414
29:41.305 --> 29:43.905
I know. I wasn't really asking you.

415
29:45.985 --> 29:48.105
And I took that job

416
29:48.185 --> 29:50.465
because I just wanted to sort out my feelings from the past

417
29:50.545 --> 29:52.305
and not leave them unresolved.

418
29:53.265 --> 29:54.625
As for him,

419
29:54.705 --> 29:56.425
whatever he thinks is his fucking business.

420
29:56.505 --> 29:58.625
I only care about my own outcome.

421
29:58.705 --> 30:00.785
What if it turns out worse than before?

422
30:00.865 --> 30:03.145
-What will you do? -You brat!

423
30:03.225 --> 30:04.905
Do I look that stupid to you?

424
30:04.985 --> 30:06.825
Take a good, long look at my face.

425
30:06.905 --> 30:08.865
I'm actually smart.

426
30:10.025 --> 30:11.145
Mm.

427
30:11.985 --> 30:13.905
You'll know when the time comes.

428
30:14.905 --> 30:17.985
And remember, some opportunities, if we don't seize them,

429
30:20.825 --> 30:21.825
they won't come again.

430
30:48.945 --> 30:50.425
There's one more song, Kao.

431
30:50.505 --> 30:52.345
It's pop rock.

432
30:52.425 --> 30:54.785
It's fun, easy on the ears, and super catchy.

433
30:54.865 --> 30:56.025
Here.

434
30:56.105 --> 30:58.425
No need. I have another meeting.

435
30:59.945 --> 31:03.385
Kao, but the song's only two or three minutes long.

436
31:07.265 --> 31:09.185
Ranne, I'll be honest.

437
31:09.265 --> 31:11.185
I don't think your band can go on like this.

438
31:15.025 --> 31:16.025
Shit.

439
31:17.185 --> 31:18.425
Feels like getting dumped.

440
31:18.985 --> 31:21.385
Of course. They're about to disband us.

441
31:23.865 --> 31:25.585
Kao, please wait.

442
31:25.665 --> 31:26.745
Kao!

443
31:27.705 --> 31:29.585
Please give us one more chance.

444
31:30.425 --> 31:32.185
We're working on a new song right now.

445
31:32.265 --> 31:33.585
-Right? -Yeah.

446
31:33.665 --> 31:35.465
A new song with a whole new sound.

447
31:35.545 --> 31:37.585
You'll definitely hear it next week.

448
31:39.065 --> 31:40.465
Enough.

449
31:40.545 --> 31:43.185
I think we've been going in circles for way too long.

450
31:44.185 --> 31:46.145
And it still hasn't clicked.

451
31:46.225 --> 31:47.825
The music needs a turning point.

452
31:48.505 --> 31:50.225
I think this is where we end.

453
31:50.825 --> 31:52.705
We'll definitely have that turning point, Kao.

454
31:52.785 --> 31:55.265
I'm trying to get a new member to join the band.

455
31:55.345 --> 31:57.985
I guarantee this person can complete our band.

456
31:58.065 --> 32:00.785
Where are they? If you've got someone, show me.

457
32:03.945 --> 32:05.305
Sorry, Kao.

458
32:05.385 --> 32:07.825
Someone's here to audition.

459
32:07.905 --> 32:09.985
He said Ranne told him to come here.

460
32:11.545 --> 32:12.465
Who?

461
32:12.545 --> 32:13.945
He said his name is Phatee.

462
32:17.505 --> 32:21.185
This is the guy, Kao. Our band's turning point.

463
32:23.465 --> 32:24.665
Really?

464
32:24.745 --> 32:26.025
Then go get him.

465
32:26.105 --> 32:27.105
Okay.

466
32:27.705 --> 32:29.185
Who the hell is he?

467
32:29.265 --> 32:30.185
Yeah.

468
32:30.265 --> 32:31.825
You'll meet him soon enough.

469
32:45.905 --> 32:46.745
Yes.

470
32:46.825 --> 32:48.225
You can introduce yourself.

471
32:49.385 --> 32:50.465
Okay.

472
32:50.545 --> 32:52.585
Hi, I'm Phatee.

473
32:57.585 --> 32:58.505
That's it?

474
33:01.785 --> 33:05.505
I play guitar and sing at a club too.

475
33:08.065 --> 33:10.065
Can you write songs too?

476
33:11.545 --> 33:12.545
A little.

477
33:14.585 --> 33:15.585
"A little."

478
33:16.585 --> 33:18.505
Let me see your basic dance moves first.

479
33:21.065 --> 33:22.105
Okay.

480
33:28.865 --> 33:30.305
Is there a problem?

481
33:32.585 --> 33:33.665
No.

482
33:40.025 --> 33:40.945
Wow.

483
33:41.025 --> 33:43.145
Come on. I'll count you in.

484
33:45.305 --> 33:48.065
Come on. I'll count you in.

485
33:48.145 --> 33:49.105
Okay, start.

486
33:49.185 --> 33:51.185
One, two, three,

487
33:51.265 --> 33:54.305
four, five, six, seven, eight.

488
33:54.385 --> 33:56.865
One, two, three, four,

489
33:56.945 --> 33:59.225
five, six, seven, eight.

490
34:08.905 --> 34:10.744
I think I've seen enough of your dancing.

491
34:10.824 --> 34:14.105
So, can you try singing?

492
34:27.545 --> 34:29.945
Can you stop pacing?

493
34:31.145 --> 34:32.425
I'm nervous.

494
34:34.344 --> 34:35.744
Look at this.

495
34:35.824 --> 34:38.304
It says we only have a 10% chance of debuting.

496
34:38.385 --> 34:40.905
By "it," you mean AI, right?

497
34:40.985 --> 34:42.585
Can you stop believing it so much?

498
34:42.665 --> 34:43.824
Have some confidence.

499
34:43.905 --> 34:45.225
Stay calm like Saw.

500
34:45.304 --> 34:46.945
Seriously?

501
34:47.744 --> 34:49.025
That's not staying calm.

502
34:49.105 --> 34:50.665
That's running away from the problem.

503
34:59.905 --> 35:01.065
Are you ready?

504
35:02.905 --> 35:04.505
If you're ready, you can start.

505
35:15.145 --> 35:18.105
Are you going to sing with your back to the audience?

506
35:21.865 --> 35:22.945
Turn around.

507
35:32.785 --> 35:34.225
Go ahead.

508
35:48.625 --> 35:49.545
Excuse me,

509
35:50.145 --> 35:51.185
Kao.

510
35:51.265 --> 35:52.505
Can I sing with him?

511
35:52.585 --> 35:54.385
Because if we end up in the same band,

512
35:54.465 --> 35:55.785
we'll have to sing together anyway.

513
35:55.865 --> 35:59.145
Go ahead. Do whatever you want. I've only got five minutes left.

514
35:59.225 --> 36:00.545
Thank you.

515
36:05.825 --> 36:06.665
Give it your all.

516
36:08.265 --> 36:10.025
You can sing the song you sing at the club.

517
36:11.145 --> 36:12.545
But it's not finished yet.

518
36:12.625 --> 36:14.065
Just sing what you have.

519
36:14.825 --> 36:15.985
Trust me.

520
36:22.025 --> 36:25.585
Then, please play the backing track.

521
36:26.585 --> 36:27.625
Okay.

522
36:35.145 --> 36:36.185
You can look at me.

523
36:58.305 --> 37:02.745
My world looks so dark and gloomy

524
37:02.825 --> 37:08.065
When people stare, I just crumble So I run away

525
37:08.145 --> 37:14.545
Far from the crowd, just me, oh, no

526
37:15.265 --> 37:18.945
I try not to feel anything

527
37:19.025 --> 37:23.185
But my heart never listens

528
37:23.265 --> 37:27.945
I can't bear it The sound of my heart's been so loud

529
37:28.025 --> 37:30.745
Ever since you came

530
37:30.825 --> 37:35.265
Too scared to say I love you

531
37:35.345 --> 37:39.185
Just being near you is enough

532
37:39.265 --> 37:43.025
I wouldn't dare to get closer to you

533
37:43.105 --> 37:49.305
But what can I do? I'm in love with you

534
37:49.385 --> 37:53.425
-Should I shout it out? -I wouldn't dare

535
37:53.505 --> 37:56.345
I wouldn't dare

536
37:57.265 --> 38:04.145
Can I whisper it softly to your ear instead?

537
38:08.945 --> 38:10.425
Ranne, how did it go?

538
38:10.505 --> 38:11.505
Did he pass?

539
38:11.585 --> 38:13.025
What did Kao say?

540
38:13.105 --> 38:14.385
I have no idea.

541
38:14.465 --> 38:16.745
As soon as we finished singing, they all left.

542
38:23.065 --> 38:24.625
I'm heading back.

543
38:24.705 --> 38:26.745
The job's done. You can pay Linda.

544
38:26.825 --> 38:28.065
Wait.

545
38:28.145 --> 38:30.825
Hold on. Aren't you staying to hear the result?

546
38:31.785 --> 38:33.065
Probably not necessary.

547
38:33.145 --> 38:35.505
I don't think anyone wants to hear someone like me sing.

548
38:35.585 --> 38:37.465
Who told you that?

549
38:37.545 --> 38:40.025
The other day, the audience was singing along with you.

550
38:40.105 --> 38:42.625
Your voice moves anyone who hears it.

551
38:43.465 --> 38:46.185
But singing for fun and singing seriously aren't the same.

552
38:46.705 --> 38:48.825
The audience probably wants to hear

553
38:48.905 --> 38:53.025
someone who can sing, dance well, and has more confidence than me.

554
38:53.105 --> 38:55.985
That was so damn good, though.

555
38:56.065 --> 38:58.665
Your voice and mine work so well together.

556
38:58.745 --> 38:59.865
Have some confidence.

557
39:02.665 --> 39:04.105
You haven't seen me dance.

558
39:09.065 --> 39:11.705
Was it that bad?

559
39:14.825 --> 39:15.985
I'll get going.

560
39:32.305 --> 39:33.305
What do we do?

561
39:35.425 --> 39:36.865
I don't know anymore.

562
39:43.345 --> 39:45.825
Oh. Where did your friend go?

563
39:45.905 --> 39:47.065
He left.

564
39:47.705 --> 39:49.065
Why did he leave?

565
39:49.145 --> 39:51.145
I rushed to get a trainee contract for him to sign.

566
39:51.225 --> 39:52.265
What?

567
39:53.305 --> 39:54.625
What do you mean?

568
39:55.225 --> 39:56.825
With a voice that good

569
39:56.905 --> 40:00.065
and chemistry this good between you and Phatee,

570
40:00.145 --> 40:01.585
I'd be stupid to let him go.

571
40:02.745 --> 40:06.185
Ranne. I found your band's selling point.

572
40:06.265 --> 40:09.545
Hurry and bring your friend back. Otherwise, your band won't get to debut.

573
40:13.545 --> 40:15.105
Hell yeah! We've got a chance!

574
40:15.185 --> 40:16.265
Hurry!

575
40:29.625 --> 40:31.385
I don't think we're going to debut.

576
40:32.065 --> 40:33.185
Hey.

577
40:33.265 --> 40:35.505
Have some hope. Hope. Can you spell it?

578
40:36.345 --> 40:37.385
I can.

579
40:37.465 --> 40:39.545
But how are you going to convince an introvert like him

580
40:39.625 --> 40:41.545
to get onstage with us?

581
40:43.145 --> 40:44.425
Hey, Ranne.

582
40:44.505 --> 40:46.385
You hired him to audition.

583
40:46.465 --> 40:49.425
Why not hire him to be a trainee at our label?

584
40:49.505 --> 40:50.745
Right.

585
40:51.385 --> 40:52.305
That's a good idea.

586
40:53.265 --> 40:54.265
I…

587
40:55.585 --> 40:56.985
I'm out of money.

588
40:59.265 --> 41:01.025
Okay, Bro. I'm going home then.

589
41:01.105 --> 41:02.385
-Stop. -Calm down.

590
41:02.945 --> 41:03.945
Sit down.

591
41:05.665 --> 41:06.705
Listen to me.

592
41:07.585 --> 41:08.585
I won't give up.

593
41:09.425 --> 41:11.545
At my age, I can't wait.

594
41:12.145 --> 41:15.505
If I don't debut this time, I probably never will.

595
41:16.105 --> 41:17.225
No matter what,

596
41:17.305 --> 41:18.505
I

597
41:19.265 --> 41:21.265
will find a way to get Phatee

598
41:21.345 --> 41:22.625
to join our band.

599
41:22.705 --> 41:23.825
How?

600
41:41.425 --> 41:43.025
You're Phatee, right?

601
41:45.105 --> 41:46.625
You sing really well.

602
41:46.705 --> 41:49.025
Can I take a photo with you? Before you get famous and I can't.

603
41:52.665 --> 41:53.985
Smile, please.

604
41:55.705 --> 41:56.625
Thank you.

605
41:59.625 --> 42:02.225
Phatee. You're famous now.

606
42:03.585 --> 42:05.225
You still don't know, do you?

607
42:05.945 --> 42:08.105
You've cut yourself off from the outside world,

608
42:08.185 --> 42:10.785
so you don't know what's going on out there.

609
42:12.065 --> 42:13.425
Look at this.

610
42:16.625 --> 42:17.705
Shit!

611
42:18.545 --> 42:19.825
This is just one clip.

612
42:19.905 --> 42:21.385
It's got millions of views.

613
42:22.105 --> 42:24.745
When you get famous, don't forget about me.

614
42:24.825 --> 42:26.785
I'll even take out the trash for you.

615
42:26.865 --> 42:29.985
I can't believe my brother's going to be a famous singer.

616
42:30.065 --> 42:31.385
No need.

617
42:33.265 --> 42:35.705
No need. By tomorrow, everyone will have forgotten.

618
42:36.585 --> 42:39.305
Aren't you going to build on this?

619
42:39.385 --> 42:41.785
The opportunity is right in front of you.

620
42:41.865 --> 42:42.705
Hey.

621
42:45.225 --> 42:47.025
-No. -What?

622
42:49.345 --> 42:50.505
Then why--

623
42:53.985 --> 42:57.025
A cloth used to wipe down a famous singer

624
42:57.105 --> 42:58.385
would definitely sell at auction.

625
43:18.505 --> 43:20.985
I know you're happy when you sing.

626
43:21.065 --> 43:23.025
If you change your mind about signing the contract,

627
43:23.105 --> 43:24.745
you can come see me.

628
43:24.825 --> 43:25.825
I'll be waiting.

629
43:57.705 --> 43:59.745
What song should we play this Valentine's Day?

630
44:01.105 --> 44:02.345
-Hey, Ble. -I--

631
44:04.505 --> 44:06.665
Play this song at the school event for me.

632
44:06.745 --> 44:07.825
I like it.

633
44:12.145 --> 44:13.585
But I can't play this song.

634
44:14.185 --> 44:16.385
Then practice it for me.

635
44:16.465 --> 44:17.705
Help me out.

636
44:17.785 --> 44:19.265
I really want this song at the school event.

637
44:23.305 --> 44:25.265
Fine! I'll try.

638
44:25.345 --> 44:26.905
Great. I'm off.

639
44:28.065 --> 44:29.465
I can't play it.

640
44:29.545 --> 44:31.025
Can you?

641
44:31.105 --> 44:32.785
I can't either. What song is this?

642
44:32.865 --> 44:34.145
Then who can we get to play it?

643
44:34.745 --> 44:35.665
Hey.

644
44:36.465 --> 44:37.465
I'll figure out the chords for you.

645
44:40.145 --> 44:41.905
Great. Thanks for helping.

646
44:41.985 --> 44:43.225
-Thanks. -Let's go.

647
44:52.345 --> 44:58.865
SECRET - PAUSE

648
46:05.385 --> 46:09.985
I’ve been looking at you for so long

649
46:10.065 --> 46:13.025
I don't dare to look

650
46:13.105 --> 46:16.105
I always have to avoid your eyes

651
46:16.185 --> 46:20.585
I’m afraid that one day

652
46:20.665 --> 46:24.145
If you find out

653
46:24.225 --> 46:27.745
The truth I’ve been hiding away

654
46:29.305 --> 46:34.705
The secret I’ve hidden I’ve never told anyone

655
46:34.785 --> 46:39.185
I don't think I can hold it back anymore

656
47:34.785 --> 47:38.665
SONGBOOK

657
47:41.785 --> 47:46.465
RANNE

658
48:00.065 --> 48:04.425
RANNE

659
48:26.985 --> 48:28.785
Your friend still hasn't gotten back to you?

660
48:31.185 --> 48:32.185
Not yet.

661
48:35.145 --> 48:36.785
Then I guess we're all on the same page.

662
48:37.985 --> 48:40.585
Tomorrow, I'll debut a new boy group.

663
48:41.345 --> 48:45.025
Anyway, thank you for all your hard work.

664
48:46.225 --> 48:47.905
I hope in the future,

665
48:47.985 --> 48:51.505
you'll find your own way to keep pursuing your dreams.

666
48:55.025 --> 48:56.105
Here.

667
48:56.185 --> 48:58.345
Sign the trainee contract termination papers,

668
48:59.065 --> 49:01.025
and you'll be free.

669
49:14.425 --> 49:15.665
I'll sign first.

670
49:16.625 --> 49:17.945
Let's get this over with.

671
49:20.625 --> 49:21.625
Ranne!

672
49:31.945 --> 49:32.945
You!

673
49:33.825 --> 49:35.825
I agree to become a trainee

674
49:36.785 --> 49:38.825
and debut with your band.

675
49:58.105 --> 49:59.905
Thanks for trusting me.

676
50:01.505 --> 50:04.345
Thank you for doing this for our dream.

677
50:12.265 --> 50:16.265
Does this mean we get to keep going?

678
50:17.865 --> 50:19.225
Yeah. We do!

679
50:20.145 --> 50:22.065
-Really? -We get to keep going!

680
50:22.145 --> 50:23.585
Really?!

681
50:24.985 --> 50:27.025
-We can keep going! -Keep going!

682
50:27.105 --> 50:28.705
We'll get to debut!

683
51:23.945 --> 51:26.065
Let's officially introduce ourselves again.

684
51:26.145 --> 51:29.665
This is Phatee. He'll be A-Team's main vocalist.

685
51:33.825 --> 51:35.025
Whose song is this?

686
51:36.425 --> 51:38.825
I was excited about the debut, but now I'm starting to worry.

687
51:38.905 --> 51:40.305
I thought he'd at least have the basics down.

688
51:40.385 --> 51:41.985
He's clearly below zero.

689
51:43.065 --> 51:44.185
Thanks for working so hard.

690
51:44.265 --> 51:47.185
I'll stay by your side and help push you forward.

691
51:47.985 --> 51:49.985
You've always been my inspiration.

692
51:51.505 --> 51:52.985
Did you know me before?
